The investigation showed that this is an issue with `svelte-language-server`, the same as described in [this comment](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1980#issuecomment-3248976104). TL;DR: it changes item's `textEdit` during 'completionItem/resolve' request, although it is explicitly must not do that. In particular for the use case described in this issue:

- Before resolve:

    ```
    textEdit = {
      newText = "{ asset$1 } from '\\$app/paths';",
      range = {
        start = { line = 5, character = 8 },
        ["end"] = { line = 6, character = 0 },
      }
    }
    ```

- After resolve:

    ```
    textEdit = {
      newText = "{ asset$1 } from '\\$app/paths';",
      range = {
        start = { line = 5, character = 8 },
        ["end"] = { line = 5, character = 11 },
      }
    }
    ```

My suggestion would be to open an issue for LSP server in particular. But since it is the second time for 'mini.completion', I've made changes to accommodate this type of misbehaving server on the "best effort basis". Should now be resolved on latest `main`.
